WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates — Week 16 Leader Video
Unit 4, Lesson 4: Story

1
00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.290
We all love a great story.

2
00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:10.250
So this lesson should be a fun one.

3
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:13.450
But I want you to remember that students need to see

4
00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:16.910
that story originates from God himself.

5
00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:19.610
Again, this is another pointer to God showing students

6
00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:23.010
that God exists because we have these things.

7
00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.830
Because we have such a thing as story,

8
00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.690
because we can tell great stories.

9
00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:29.050
And as people that reflect the image of God,

10
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:32.570
we get that from him.

11
00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.130
And it's awesome.

12
00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:35.890
And your students hopefully will see that

13
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:37.970
at the end of this unit.

14
00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.530
And a fun way to do this is to find different stories,

15
00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.570
whether it be your own story,

16
00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:43.850
or maybe some of their stories,

17
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.210
or someone that you know,

18
00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.350
could be a book, could be a movie.

19
00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.330
But you want to find within those stories,

20
00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:51.650
redemptive themes, themes of salvation,

21
00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:52.650
those kinds of things.

22
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:56.970
And you'd be surprised how many different stories

23
00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:58.610
are actually based off of

24
00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:02.050
or have biblical themes buried within them.

25
00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:07.090
So now you are officially halfway through the curriculum.

26
00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:11.010
You've had some time to take inventory of where you are,

27
00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.850
